## What to build

A coordinator can enter manual destination details when scheduling or rescheduling Beginners' Workshops, and the person can find directions on their existing workshop-place page. Saving destination-only enrichment at the same Venue must not announce a reschedule or alter workshop policy. Reuse the shared destination input while keeping this domain's storage and commands independent.

Publishing this ticket specifies later work; it does not start implementation or authorize Google provisioning, billing/key changes, production activation or production backfill. Obtain implementation authorization before code changes, and separate operational authorization before any live Google or production work.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Add nullable destination storage, schedule/reschedule requests, workshop reads and the closed safe Intake view through the domain's own contracts. Preserve the required short label's 80-character maximum; a full address does not belong in the email label. Existing rows and label-only submissions remain valid.
- [ ] Reuse the domain-neutral destination input in schedule/reschedule, preserving remote-form names, values and field errors, keyboard access and phone usability. Shared values apply to every date in multi-date scheduling, with each workshop owning its saved destination.
- [ ] Keep every write behind BeginnersWorkshops.execute/3 and the existing Schedule family/protocol locks. Add a distinct, authorized same-Venue destination-enrichment command rather than sending destination-only updates through reschedule_workshop.
- [ ] The form's source-owned operation distinguishes destination-only enrichment from a genuine reschedule. Enrichment changes no label, date/time, payment deadline, offer-round/window state, reschedule counter or reschedule history and queues no rescheduled Intake Email or rescheduled Staff Notification. Frontend suppression of emails is not the rule.
- [ ] Genuine permitted rescheduling continues through the existing command and retains its current deadline, history, email and Staff-notification behaviour. Do not merge source contexts or create a new scheduling/payment writer.
- [ ] Preserve saved destinations on omission and unrelated changes; support explicit replacement and clear. Apply authoritative field errors and safe HTTPS Maps-link validation. Manual scheduling works without Places or any provider call.
- [ ] Render label, destination and safe directions on the existing Intake page, with legacy fallback and no new public Beginners' Workshop listing. Preserve no-referrer responses and referrer-safe navigation; private Intake tokens/URLs must not enter Google requests or directions queries.
- [ ] Extend the domain-owned Calendar projection and record identifier-only intent in the same transaction. Both audiences use native location through the existing protocol, preserving event identity, RSVPs, normal meaningful-update notifications, silent no-ops, existing historical cutoffs and explicit activation.
- [ ] Cover real schedule/reschedule and destination-only form submissions through browser/E2E and Phoenix, multi-date persistence, the 80-character limit, invalid/manual URLs, omission/clear, rejection recovery and safe attendee reads. Assert unchanged source facts, email log occasions/jobs and Staff notifications for enrichment; retain genuine-reschedule regression coverage.
- [ ] Drive public commands and Calendar sync with real persistence, fixed boundary clocks and Req.Test Google/OAuth. Assert both Calendar audiences' locations and privacy, normal update parameters and unchanged place/payment/refund/attendance semantics.

